Context
  Directed to treat ~/.guile-skill/projects/<slug>/ as deprecated in favour of
  the sanctioned ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}, after the developer guides turned up the
  convention we had reinvented.

Considerations
  - The three path variables are documented as resolving inline in Markdown
    bodies, and explicitly NOT exported to the Bash tool's environment. A design
    that had the scripts read $CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA themselves would appear to
    work in a hook or an MCP server and silently fall back everywhere else. The
    handover via GUILE_SKILL_DATA is what makes the substitution the single
    source.
  - ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} is deleted on plugin uninstall unless --keep-data,
    where ~/.guile-skill survived. For REPL transcripts -- which contain
    whatever was evaluated -- deletion on uninstall is defensible, arguably
    better. Recorded because it is a real semantic change, not a free swap.
  - The fallback is kept rather than a hard cutover so an existing checkout
    keeps finding its old transcripts. `guile-repl-paths.sh' marks the fallback
    DEPRECATED in its report so the choice is visible.

Deviations
  - No new flags on any bin/*.sh script; the data root arrives by environment
    variable. That keeps the argument contracts untouched, so this stays below
    the major bar in RELEASING.md while still adding a supported configuration.
  - evals/stale-listener/prompt.md was edited despite the top-level evals/ being
    out of scope earlier in this work: it names the transcript path, and leaving
    it pointing at the deprecated location would make the eval test the wrong
    thing.
